{"title":"1966 AHSME Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is real and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/3/523e6bf7f260f3cac2cb1a3fe88a35f4f2ff4d33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4y^2+4xy+x+6=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"174\" height=\"18\" />, then the complete set of values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is real, is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/9/8f927c61cffb1a33270ba32c4beb5cf8ebb62e08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } x\\le-2 \\text{ or } x\\ge3 \\quad \\text{(B) }  x\\le2 \\text{ or } x\\ge3 \\quad \\text{(C) }  x\\le-3 \\text{ or } x\\ge2 \\quad \\\\ \\text{(D) } -3\\le x\\le2 \\quad \\text{(E) } -2\\le x\\le3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"492\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We treat the equation as a quadratic equation in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> for which the discriminant \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/85505f1639cbb612a29ee8785680a2e373ffc556.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[D=16x^2-16(x+6)=16(x^2-x-6)=16(x-3)(x+2)\\]\" width=\"462\" height=\"19\" /> \nFor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to be real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/2/1e2df7cf2517096d57375581e287280aa46598ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />. This inequality is satisfied when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/c/0acdef1ac3d4ec117a87d202fea1585077448182.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\le -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/b/ceb7e9048c55a797019c9afa3d4298726e724fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\ge3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386255c1da145bc497cf598169ccbaa210e8d0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=